  reel_script says the constable was injured/driving 'to the police station' as a fact-consistent detail, but the reel_script omits that the driver Vijay was drunk being the reason the van was taken over — acceptable; however reel_script states the van was 'பிடிபட்ட' (caught) at Musiri without the article's detail that the van was seized during a check; minor. Main problem: slides_spec 'என்ன நடந்தது' says the van was taken to the police station by the constable, but slides_spec 'எங்கே' line says the check happened at 'குளித்தலை–முசிறி இணைக்கும் பெரியார் பாலம் அருகே' while the article says the check was near Periyar bridge, which is fine; however the caption and reel_script state the constable drove the van 'to the police station' and the reel_script omits that the owner Manickavasagam opposed the seizure, and the caption's 'போலீசார்' attribution of the 'பேச்சுவார்த்தை' to 'தொட்டியம் போலீசார்' is correct, but the reel_script says 'தொட்டியம் போலீசார் பேச்சுவார்த்தை நடத்தியதால் போராட்டம் கைவிடப்பட்டது' which is accurate. Also the reel_script omits that the driver was in a drunk state at the time of the check as the cause; it states it, so ok. Key issue: the reel_script and slides say the constable was injured 'காயமடைந்தார்' correctly, but the reel_script's sentence 'காவலர் மருதமுத்து காயமடைந்தார்' is preceded by 'காவலர்' driving 'to the police station' with no mention of the accident location and the caption/reel_script omit the location 'சந்தப்பாளையம்' in the reel_script, which is an important place detail missing.
